#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186244002 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124486 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdde35e9-7101-55f2-8452-ec1ef2d17d54" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Coefficients That Show Linear Dependence Among Matrix Vectors"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "49d475c3-b810-5805-a728-6b8e415a295a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241848} {:answer/id #uuid "c1800049-e113-556d-8f09-7fe35fa6d8eb" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The set is linearly independent" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242875} {:answer/id #uuid "e29bca57-c8c4-5b31-9572-c5f5f5ffea32" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243193} {:answer/id #uuid "ef6ae3c3-a0bc-5532-b547-370e5408512c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243303} {:answer/id #uuid "ff7406ef-209e-58ee-a0b5-87bffe92acce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243429}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "49d475c3-b810-5805-a728-6b8e415a295a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241848} :answer-field/id #uuid "ccdc138e-bb95-5aaf-8e12-5fa2bad487bc" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243797}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "20f026a9-c929-5f67-a8ba-c0d4cc456de0" :question/math-academy-id "q-107031" :question/problem "Consider the set of matrices $\\{A,B,C\\},$ where \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}],\\,B=[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}],\\,C=[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\n \nIf the set is linearly dependent, find the value of $\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}$ from a non-zero solution of ${x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O,$ where $O$ is the $2\\times 2$ zero-matrix." :question/worked-solution "If the set is linearly dependent, then there exist ${x}_{1},{x}_{2},{x}_{3}$ not all zero such that \n\n$$\n{x}_{1}A+{x}_{2}B+{x}_{3}C=O.\n$$\n\nOtherwise, if ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=0,$ the set is linearly independent.\n\nSubstituting the matrices $A,$ $B,$ and $C$ into the above equation, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & -2\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{2}[\\begin{aligned}-3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 4\\end{aligned}]+{x}_{3}[\\begin{aligned}4 & -4 \\\\ -8 & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} & {x}_{1} \\\\ 0 & -2{x}_{1}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-3{x}_{2} & -{x}_{2} \\\\ 2{x}_{2} & 4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}4{x}_{3} & -4{x}_{3} \\\\ -8{x}_{3} & 0\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] \\\\ [\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3} & {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3} \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3} & -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEquating the corresponding entries, we obtain the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ {x}_{1}-{x}_{2}-4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ -2{x}_{1}+4{x}_{2}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we consider the corresponding augmented matrix and reduce it to row echelon form using Gaussian elimination:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 1 & -1 & -4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 4 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+(-1){R}_{1} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+2{R}_{1}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2 & 8 & 0\\end{aligned}] &  & \\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+(-1){R}_{2} \\\\ {R}_{4}:={R}_{4}+{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 4 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & -8 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe pivot columns are the $1$st and $2$nd.\nHence, ${x}_{3}$ is a free variable.\n\nThe system is now\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1}-3{x}_{2}+4{x}_{3}=0 \\\\ 2{x}_{2}-8{x}_{3}=0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the $2$nd equation, we get ${x}_{2}=4{x}_{3}.$ Substitute it into the first equation to get\n\n$$\n{x}_{1}-3(4{x}_{3})+4{x}_{3}=0\\,⟹\\,{x}_{1}=8{x}_{3}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, the general solution is \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}{x}_{1} \\\\ {x}_{2} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}8{x}_{3} \\\\ 4{x}_{3} \\\\ {x}_{3}\\end{aligned}],\\,{x}_{3}\\in R.\n$$\n\nFinally, for any ${x}_{3}\\ne 0,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}_{1}}{{x}_{2}}=\\frac{8{x}_{3}}{4{x}_{3}}=2.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186247185 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186119810 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5c8e217c-252d-529f-a810-84787e2ee886" :knowledge-point/title "Determining if a Vector is in the Column Space of a Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5afd7296-0e41-5a52-8705-c7c0fbb42d4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245110} {:answer/id #uuid "6432d9a5-cb06-5009-a488-f5f4aca2c370" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245195} {:answer/id #uuid "64fbeade-a556-57de-b9d8-c66b01089ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245207} {:answer/id #uuid "a639644e-969e-5af1-8ddb-b741ba91a374" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245801} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c696c1-ce2c-55ff-89ef-065b9ea5e562" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246330}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "64fbeade-a556-57de-b9d8-c66b01089ebc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "b\\notin \\text{Col}(C)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186245207} :answer-field/id #uuid "bf8f671a-ae62-58c4-8bc0-0e675cc16311" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186246892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7005444a-a247-5177-8b52-a944d472324a" :question/math-academy-id "q-110969" :question/problem "The matrix $C$ and the vector $b$ are given below. Determine if $b\\in \\text{Col}(C).$ In the affirmative case, find the value of ${x}_{1}+{x}_{2}$, where ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are real numbers such that $b={x}_{1}{c}_{1}+{x}_{2}{c}_{2},$ and ${c}_{1},$ ${c}_{2}$ are the respective columns of $C.$\n\n$$\nC=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & -3\\end{aligned}],\\,b=[\\begin{aligned}9 \\\\ -15\\end{aligned}]\n$$" :question/worked-solution "In order to determine whether $b$ lies in $\\text{Col}(C),$ we need to check if the equation $Cx=b$ is consistent. So, let's find the row echelon form of the augmented matrix $[C\\,|\\,b]$ as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[C\\,|\\,b] & =[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 3 & -3 & -15\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 1 & 9 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 12\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we have the system\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}-{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}=9 \\\\ 0=12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the second equation, we get the false statement $0=12.$  \n\nTherefore, the system is inconsistent, which implies that $b\\notin \\text{Col}(C).$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186262576 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192754 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "1fdf4f96-f679-57b8-96aa-7e9c34b986b8" :knowledge-point/title "Computing a Probability Over an Unbounded Interval"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e12cbba-3631-54d1-84d7-964542214c91" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260005} {:answer/id #uuid "807da1aa-15ec-597d-9ce5-8ad32b6f43db" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{e}^{-3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186260993} {:answer/id #uuid "96728374-4c7e-5993-8514-03f9bcc34be0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261179} {:answer/id #uuid "b9d9e748-5a09-5259-ae66-914ca28c408d" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261503} {:answer/id #uuid "c42d6103-4d6c-587b-81f1-697d7b6da448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261604}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c42d6103-4d6c-587b-81f1-697d7b6da448" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{e}^{-1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186261604} :answer-field/id #uuid "c33853e1-0a4c-5b0b-b820-5e3dbbe949b2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186262474}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "e72b6d0d-48ab-5023-98ff-ea2cdd5bb4d7" :question/math-academy-id "q-126016" :question/problem "Compute $P(X\\ge 3)$ given that the random variable $X$ has the probability density function\n\n$$\nf(x)=\\{\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x},\\, & x\\ge 0, \\\\ 0,\\, & x<0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "If a continuous random variable $X$ has the probability density function $f(x),$ then \n\n$$\nP(a<X<b)={\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nSo, in our case, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(X\\ge 3) & =P(3\\le X<\\infty ) \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\int }_{3}^{\\infty }\\frac{1}{3}{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={[-{e}^{-\\frac{1}{3}x}]}_{3}^{\\infty } \\\\  & ={e}^{-1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186398375 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186115249 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "b7f42188-bf51-5546-89fb-e33ba47c4b5e" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Row Operations Required To Find the Inverse of a 2x2 Matrix"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "92b6e22e-e14f-536e-a8cf-ab5edfb0d027" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398377} {:answer/id #uuid "3f468114-a837-5315-9463-743e098f65ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398378} {:answer/id #uuid "3540d783-48ba-526c-a122-0ebe4bb9b9be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398379} {:answer/id #uuid "dd01665e-3643-581b-8e10-6bc426a9baba" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398380} {:answer/id #uuid "8a98a201-ff8f-5c9f-a6de-5a59d7503724" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}-2{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398381}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3540d783-48ba-526c-a122-0ebe4bb9b9be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398379} :answer-field/id #uuid "89863539-4901-5ced-a4bc-1a69933efb51" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186398376}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "41dc19c4-f697-52b3-b9b5-76ded5157f14" :question/math-academy-id "q-131999" :question/problem "The inverse of the matrix $Y$ is found using row operations, as shown below. What are the row operations corresponding to each step?\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Y\\,|\\,I] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] &  & \\text{___________} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We write down $Y$ and the identity matrix $I$ side-by-side (as shown below) and apply the standard Gauss-Jordan method to transform the matrix $Y$ into the identity matrix. We perform the same row operations on both matrices:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[Y\\,|\\,I\\,] & =[\\begin{aligned}4 & -1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :={R}_{1}+{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -3 & 1 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe corresponding row operations are\n\n$$\n{R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+{R}_{2},\\,{R}_{2}:={R}_{2}+3{R}_{1}.\n$$\n\nThe matrix ${Y}^{-1}$ is given by the right-hand side of our big matrix after all of the transformations have been completed. Therefore, \n\n$$\n{Y}^{-1}=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186488217 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162105 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "277b8807-fb74-5ad3-a89b-92dbf90bc075" :knowledge-point/title "Computing the Value of a Conditional Probability Mass Function at a Point"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "00e65e89-b6a1-56e9-bd5e-da67acd6079c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487569} {:answer/id #uuid "1f6777e1-b57b-5667-bba3-1a26c27e63e3" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487633} {:answer/id #uuid "59872684-ab61-548c-a315-d38040730c82" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487747} {:answer/id #uuid "c5842798-b8d9-5edc-85f3-9c23e26a0409" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186487942} {:answer/id #uuid "f1b05117-82ad-54b2-b2bb-0dd42a0b1a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "f1b05117-82ad-54b2-b2bb-0dd42a0b1a3a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488019} :answer-field/id #uuid "d5318616-df05-5cb7-9c1a-585554d2944f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186488151}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "654ece2b-abda-569c-8738-da98c426c46e" :question/math-academy-id "q-142891" :question/problem "| $f$ | $Y=2$ | $Y=4$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $X=1$ | $\\frac{3}{20}$ | $\\frac{7}{20}$ |\n| $X=3$ | $\\frac{9}{20}$ | $\\frac{1}{20}$ |\n\nCompute ${f}_{Y|X}(2\\,|\\,3)$ given that the discrete random variables $X$ and $Y$ have the joint probability mass function $f(x,y)$ shown in the table above." :question/worked-solution "The conditional probability mass function ${f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)$ is defined as\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(y\\,|\\,x)=P(Y=y\\,|\\,X=x).\n$$\n\nTherefore, we're required to compute the conditional probability\n\n$$\n{f}_{Y|X}(2\\,|\\,3)=P(Y=2\\,|\\,X=3).\n$$\n\nBy the multiplication law for conditional probability, we have\n\n$$\nP(Y=2\\,|\\,X=3)=\\frac{P(X=3,Y=2)}{P(X=3)}=\\frac{f(3,2)}{{f}_{X}(3)}\n$$\n\nwhere $f(x,y)$ is the joint probability mass function of $X$ and $Y,$ and ${f}_{X}(x)$ is the marginal distribution of $X.$\n\nRecall that the marginal distribution for $X$ corresponds to the row totals. Thus, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{X}(3) & =f(3,2)+f(3,4) \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{20}+\\frac{1}{20} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom the given table, $f(3,2)=\\frac{9}{20}.$ \n\nFinally, substituting  ${f}_{X}(3)=\\frac{1}{2}$ and $f(3,2)=\\frac{9}{20}$ in our formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{Y|X}(2\\,|\\,3) & =P(Y=2\\,|\\,X=3) \\\\  & =\\frac{f(3,2)}{{f}_{X}(3)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(\\frac{9}{20})}{(\\frac{1}{2})} \\\\  & =\\frac{9}{10}.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186435686 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186192802 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e534c006-a5b4-5f76-bbd6-451496358d3a" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Boundary of a Set"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "12dc85bb-cd47-5b33-a127-8e0086b71833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y<2-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435680} {:answer/id #uuid "4abb66be-2678-58be-a9b9-2a2311d4b784" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y>2-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435681} {:answer/id #uuid "4f38e133-dcd8-5339-a2b7-5a9997c0d1f0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\le 2-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435682} {:answer/id #uuid "6dc57868-eec7-5486-9156-13dad63ee061" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y\\ge 2-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435683} {:answer/id #uuid "db118f09-f7c6-5463-ab93-b46db354c131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435684}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "db118f09-f7c6-5463-ab93-b46db354c131" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "y=2-x" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435684} :answer-field/id #uuid "4437d06f-222c-582a-ab1b-38dd45632e8b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186435685}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4bf3edf8-7469-5b33-bc3b-54f4acae6cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161595" :question/problem "![](images/65/6559dfed58b9456d6eebfd660f7a0d59a60db9db1159561f010f6b7e13e90e5b.png)\n\nConsider the set $A,$ shown above. The boundary of $A$ is given by\n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,\\bbox[5px,border:1px solid black]{\\phantom{AAAAA}}\\,\\}.\n$$\n\nWhat is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "The boundary of a set $A,$ denoted $∂A,$ is the set that contains all the boundary points of $A.$\n\nThe set $A$ and its boundary $∂A$ are shown below.\n\n![](images/d7/d7293d96b71f573dbdcbfb491646f0e563f8ad1567eab5baaf960533e72d473f.png)\n\nFrom the diagram, the boundary points of $A$ lie on the line $y=2-x.$\n\nTherefore, \n\n$$\n∂A=\\{(x,y)\\in {R}^{2}\\,:\\,y=2-x\\,\\}.\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186148197 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186147427 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "a19140af-1870-5dee-86a2-6052451803d4" :knowledge-point/title "Identifying the Intersection of Two Planes"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e6f4d22-2c99-5542-928b-c3b59936dc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448732} {:answer/id #uuid "d5c58bba-fadc-524a-a8cc-494b4f99f03b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448733}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e6f4d22-2c99-5542-928b-c3b59936dc5e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448732} :answer-field/id #uuid "7a296daa-ab96-5c4a-a1f8-b78ea1e385cb" :answer-field/key "I" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449406} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "16084eea-535d-5acb-adce-4de2cf9e9675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448734} {:answer/id #uuid "0f60ff85-a36c-5de6-b1ed-084a5b496106" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448735}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16084eea-535d-5acb-adce-4de2cf9e9675" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448734} :answer-field/id #uuid "29d97c3e-8aa9-51c8-a4d7-7e07197c935d" :answer-field/key "II" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449407} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "adc0e532-ce8f-5ce5-ad6d-bd6230d11a37" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448736} {:answer/id #uuid "d0817e09-8e2c-5a3f-ab83-e7c67840909f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448737}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d0817e09-8e2c-5a3f-ab83-e7c67840909f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186448737} :answer-field/id #uuid "c388eae4-2ad8-5c93-87d1-98e87cfacc3b" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186449408}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "ddee53f3-5b0d-5dc0-9b9e-825db292f3e5" :question/math-academy-id "q-71110" :question/problem "Given the two planes $3x-y+z=0$ and $x-z+4=0$, which of the following statements are true?\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** The cross product of the normal vectors of the planes is equal to $0.$\n- **II.** The planes are parallel.\n- **III.** The planes intersect on a line." :question/worked-solution "First, notice that:\n\n- For the plane $3x-y+z=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{1}=⟨3,-1,1⟩.$\n\n- For the plane $x-z+4=0,$ a normal vector to the plane is ${n}_{2}=⟨1,0,-1⟩.$\n\nNow, let's consider the statements.\n\n- Statement I is false. Computing the cross product of the normal vectors, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2} & =⟨3,-1,1⟩\\times ⟨1,0,-1⟩ \\\\  & =\\left|\\begin{aligned}i & j & k \\\\ 3 & -1 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}\\right| \\\\  & =i+4j+k \\\\  & =⟨1,4,1⟩\\ne 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- Statement II is false. Since ${n}_{1}\\times {n}_{2}\\ne 0$, the vectors ${n}_{1}$ and ${n}_{2}$ are not parallel. As a result, the planes are not parallel either.\n\n- Statement III is true. Indeed, two non-parallel planes in $3$-dimensional space must intersect on a line.\n\nTherefore, only statement III is true."}]}
